# ========== NODE MODULES ==========
# NPM packages (huge folder, can be reinstalled with 'npm install')
node_modules/

# ========== ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES ==========
# Contains secrets like database passwords
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.test

# ========== LOGS ==========
# Log files generated during development/production
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ========== OPERATING SYSTEM FILES ==========
# Mac
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini

# Linux
*~
.directory

# ========== IDE / EDITOR FILES ==========
# VS Code
.vscode/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

# WebStorm / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Sublime Text
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# ========== BUILD / DIST FOLDERS ==========
# Compiled output
dist/
build/
out/

# ========== TESTING ==========
# Test coverage reports
coverage/
*.coverage
.nyc_output/

# ========== DATABASE FILES ==========
# SQLite files (if you ever use SQLite for testing)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ========== TEMPORARY FILES ==========
# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ========== MISC ==========
# Lock files (optional - some teams commit these)
# Uncomment if you want to ignore them
# package-lock.json
# yarn.lock
# pnpm-lock.yaml

# Other
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
```

---

## 🤔 **Why Each Section Matters**

### **node_modules/**
```
Size: 100-300 MB
Reason: Can reinstall with 'npm install'
Never commit this!
```

### **.env**
```
Contains: Database passwords, API keys, secrets
Reason: Security - never expose passwords
Alternative: Use .env.example (without real values)
```

### **Logs**
```
Contains: Error logs, debug info
Reason: Generated files, not needed in repo
Can regenerate anytime
```

### **OS Files**
```
.DS_Store (Mac): Folder settings
Thumbs.db (Windows): Thumbnail cache
Reason: Not related to your project
```

### **IDE Files**
```
.vscode/, .idea/: Editor settings
Reason: Personal preferences
Each developer has their own setup